; Not built in this workspace. This backend reaches the switch's cohttp, which
; was compiled against the switch's base64, while vendor/base64 shadows base64
; for the whole workspace. Two base64 libraries in one link is what dune
; reports as a conflict. Vendoring cohttp as well would settle it, which is a
; large dependency to carry for a backend nothing here uses: every consumer in
; this tree takes fetch-curl. The sources stay so the package remains complete
; for its own repository.
(library
 (name fetch_cohttp)
 (public_name fetch-cohttp)
 (enabled_if false)
 (libraries fetch fetch.cookies eio http uri cohttp-eio decompress.de
   decompress.gz fmt))
